**Critical Finding**: **Learning-focused use dominates** (75% vs. 62% for pure creativity). Participants primarily see platform as **educational tool for technique acquisition**, surpassing creative-expression purposes.

**Pedagogical Implication**: This suggests the platform's greatest value proposition is not "creative muse" but "writing instructor." Users want to learn poetic craft, use AI as scaffolding for skill development. This reframes marketing and design priorities away from "creative inspiration" toward "guided learning."

