## FINDING 13: Data Quality & Research Insights

**Methodological Strengths of Phase 2:**
- **Ecological validity**: Naturalistic voluntary context captures authentic use patterns
- **Response rate**: 89% feedback completion (8/8 survey submissions)
- **Multi-source triangulation**: Chat histories + feedback forms + panel discussion + artifacts
- **Rich interaction data**: 30-50 message exchanges per participant enable mechanism analysis

**Limitations & Clarifications:**
- One participant (Zhu Ying Lam/p 13) gave 5/5 ratings but expressed unlikely future use—disconnect between one-time satisfaction and sustained utility suggests distinction between "enjoyment of experience" and "perceived ongoing utility"
- Survey interpretation inconsistency (e.g., p 13 checked all 9 use cases yet uncertain about future use)—suggests some respondents may have over-selected or misunderstood questions
- Participant anonymization: Survey codes (p 11-p 19) don't always align with transcribed names—verification needed for data integrity

**Recommendation**: Conduct brief follow-up interviews with participants, especially those showing disconnect between satisfaction and use intention, to clarify motivational patterns.

